<!-- ═══ §01 THE PROBLEM ═══ -->
<section id="s-intro" data-code="intro">
<div class="section-no">01 — The Two-Tokenizer Trap</div>
<h2>Unified models that aren't quite unified</h2>

<p>The dream of a unified multimodal model is simple: one model that can both understand and generate images — and can <em>reason about what it just created</em>. In practice, almost every model calling itself "unified" hides an uncomfortable split.</p>

<p>Visual understanding and generation have historically required incompatible representations. Understanding tasks benefit from <strong>high-level semantic features</strong> — the kind a contrastively-trained ViT like SigLIP produces, where "cat" and "kitten" are nearby in embedding space. Generation tasks need <strong>low-level pixel details</strong> — texture frequencies, color gradients — captured by reconstruction-oriented VQ-VAEs trained to minimize pixel error.</p>

<p>So when a model like BAGEL or Janus-Pro "generates" an image then "understands" it, two separate visual tokenizers are involved. The generation uses VQ tokens; the understanding path re-encodes the rendered pixels through the semantic ViT. The model never actually reads its own generated tokens — it reads a fresh encoding of the rendered image.</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">The context gap: two tokenizers vs one shared context</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <svg id="svg-architecture" viewBox="0 0 680 280" style="width:100%;max-width:680px;display:block;margin:0 auto;font-family:var(--ff-mono)">
      <!-- LEFT: DUAL TOKENIZER -->
      <text x="165" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#6b7280" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="1">EXISTING UNIFIED MODELS</text>

      <!-- Understanding path -->
      <rect x="10" y="35" width="100" height="32" rx="5" fill="rgba(6,182,212,.12)" stroke="#06b6d4" stroke-width="1"/>
      <text x="60" y="55" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#06b6d4">Semantic ViT</text>
      <text x="60" y="64" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#6b7280">(SigLIP)</text>

      <!-- Generation path -->
      <rect x="10" y="105" width="100" height="32" rx="5" fill="rgba(245,158,11,.12)" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1"/>
      <text x="60" y="125" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#f59e0b">VQ-VAE</text>
      <text x="60" y="134" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#6b7280">(generation)</text>

      <!-- LLM backbone -->
      <rect x="145" y="65" width="80" height="42" rx="5" fill="rgba(139,92,246,.12)" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="1"/>
      <text x="185" y="83" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#8b5cf6">LLM</text>
      <text x="185" y="94" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#6b7280">backbone</text>
      <text x="185" y="103" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#6b7280">(next-token)</text>

      <!-- Rendered image -->
      <rect x="255" y="100" width="60" height="32" rx="5" fill="rgba(255,255,255,.05)" stroke="#374151" stroke-width="1"/>
      <text x="285" y="120" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#9ca3af">Rendered</text>
      <text x="285" y="129" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#6b7280">image</text>

      <!-- RE-ENCODE arrow (red) -->
      <path d="M315 116 Q355 116 355 67 Q355 55 335 51" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" stroke-dasharray="4,2"/>
      <text x="358" y="88" font-size="8" fill="#ef4444">re-encode</text>
      <text x="358" y="98" font-size="7.5" fill="#6b7280">(extra pass)</text>
      <polygon points="130,52 120,48 120,56" fill="#ef4444"/>

      <!-- Arrows: semantic → LLM -->
      <line x1="110" y1="51" x2="145" y2="75" stroke="#06b6d4" stroke-width="1.2"/>
      <polygon points="145,75 135,68 139,78" fill="#06b6d4"/>

      <!-- Arrows: VQ-VAE → LLM -->
      <line x1="110" y1="121" x2="145" y2="101" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
      <polygon points="145,101 137,112 147,110" fill="#f59e0b"/>

      <!-- LLM → rendered -->
      <line x1="225" y1="90" x2="255" y2="116" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="1.2"/>
      <polygon points="255,116 245,108 249,119" fill="#8b5cf6"/>

      <!-- X gap marker -->
      <text x="185" y="195" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#ef4444">✗ shared context broken</text>
      <text x="185" y="210" text-anchor="middle" font-size="8.5" fill="#6b7280">generated tokens ≠ understanding tokens</text>

      <!-- DIVIDER -->
      <line x1="340" y1="0" x2="340" y2="280" stroke="#1f2937" stroke-width="1.5"/>

      <!-- RIGHT: UNIAR -->
      <text x="510" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#6b7280" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="1">UNIAR</text>

      <!-- Single BSQ tokenizer -->
      <rect x="360" y="70" width="110" height="42" rx="5" fill="rgba(16,185,129,.12)" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="415" y="88" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#10b981">Single BSQ</text>
      <text x="415" y="98" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#10b981">Tokenizer</text>
      <text x="415" y="108" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#6b7280">shallow + deep features</text>

      <!-- LLM backbone -->
      <rect x="500" y="70" width="80" height="42" rx="5" fill="rgba(139,92,246,.12)" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="1"/>
      <text x="540" y="88" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#8b5cf6">LLM</text>
      <text x="540" y="98" text-anchor="middle" font-size="7.5" fill="#6b7280">backbone</text>
